     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><span style=\"background-color:rgb(244,204,204)\">My idea is: add a dynamic text in header of dashboard. </span> <font color=\"#000000\" style=\"background-color:rgb(255,0,0)\">Text Here</font><div><font color=\"#000000\"><div style=\"border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px;word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250)\">body &lt;- dashboardBody(</div><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250)\">    useShinyjs(),</div><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250)\">    # This will call message-handler.js</div><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250)\">    tags$head(tags$script(src = &quot;js/alert_message.js&quot;),</div><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250)\">              tags$link(rel = &quot;stylesheet&quot;, type = &quot;text/css&quot;, href = &quot;css/tmod.css&quot;)),</div><div><span style=\"background-color:rgb(147,196,125)\">    tags$script(HTML(&#39;$(document).ready(function() {</span></div><div><span style=\"background-color:rgb(147,196,125)\">                     $(&quot;header&quot;).find(&quot;nav&quot;).append(\\&#39;&lt;span class=&quot;myClass&quot;&gt; Text Here &lt;/span&gt;\\&#39;);</span></div><div><span style=\"background-color:rgb(147,196,125)\">                     })</span></div><div><span style=\"background-color:rgb(147,196,125)\">                     &#39;)),</span></div><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250)\">    tabItems(</div><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250)\">        tabItem(tabName = &quot;file_preview&quot;,</div></div></code></div><span style=\"background-color:rgb(244,204,204)\">The green area is how I add &quot;Text Here&quot; in header.  Of course, it is not dynamic text.</span><br></font></div><div><p style=\"text-align:center;clear:both\"><a href=\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/-uMHo23KetHo/WZ37hA92dII/AAAAAAAAEAA/uqVz2yfIOHca1LjHxIou9lNjYUnMhaNwgCLcBGAs/s1600/Screen%2BShot%2B2017-08-24%2Bat%2B00.02.13.png\" style=\"margin-left:1em;margin-right:1em\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/-uMHo23KetHo/WZ37hA92dII/AAAAAAAAEAA/uqVz2yfIOHca1LjHxIou9lNjYUnMhaNwgCLcBGAs/s1600/Screen%252BShot%252B2017-08-24%252Bat%252B00.02.13.png&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792389087865000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0c3NY4A7FzsMiu_EBUClzi\"><img src=\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/-uMHo23KetHo/WZ37hA92dII/AAAAAAAAEAA/uqVz2yfIOHca1LjHxIou9lNjYUnMhaNwgCLcBGAs/s1600/Screen%2BShot%2B2017-08-24%2Bat%2B00.02.13.png\" border=\"0\"></a></p><div><span style=\"background-color:rgb(244,204,204)\"> Now, I try to split the code chunk into an independent js file. I have </span><span style=\"background-color:rgb(182,215,168)\">alert_message.js</span>. Try to be dynamic!</div></div><div><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px;word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><div>Shiny.addCustomMessageHandler(&quot;header_message&quot;,</div><div><span style=\"white-space:pre\">\t</span>function(headerMessage){</div><div><span style=\"white-space:pre\">\t\t</span>$(&quot;header&quot;).find(&quot;nav&quot;).append(&#39;&lt;span  class=&quot;myClass&quot;&gt; Text Here&lt;/span&gt;&#39;, headerMessage)</div><div><span style=\"white-space:pre\">\t</span>}</div><div>);<br><br></div><div><br></div></div></code></div><div style=\"border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px;word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><div><span style=\"background-color:rgb(244,204,204)\"># in server.R, I try to call js function. But it does not show any thing.</span><span style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250)\"> </span><br><br><span style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250)\">observe({</span></div><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250)\">        input$run</div><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250)\">        mess &lt;- &quot;I am worried about you&quot;</div><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250)\">        session$sendCustomMessage(type=&quot;header_message&quot;, mess)</div><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250)\">    })</div></div></code></div><br><div><b><font color=\"#000000\" style=\"background-color:rgb(244,204,204)\">Are there any mistakes in my jsFile or R file?</font></b></div><div><br></div><div>Thank you!</div><div>Song</div><br><br></div><div><br></div><div><br></div></div>"
